# --- fonts ---------------------------------------------------------------
# EXACTLY viacoffee/dotfiles' set, no more and no less, and that is deliberate.
# /usr/lib/initcpio/install/plymouth resolves the font it embeds in the initramfs
# with `fc-match`, and neither his theme nor ours sets `Font =` in its .plymouth
# file — so the font Plymouth ends up with is decided by whatever happens to be
# installed on the build machine. This repo's password dialog was rendering once
# and never updating on a machine whose only font package was noto-fonts-emoji.
#
# Held back until a real boot is seen working, then re-add one at a time:
#   noto-fonts-emoji   (emoji in waybar, mako, the terminal)
#   noto-fonts-cjk     (CJK text renders as boxes without it)
#   Fragment Mono      (assets/fonts/, the terminal font this repo picked;
#                       packaged in the AUR as ttf-fragment-mono)
noto-fonts
ttf-dejavu
ttf-liberation
ttf-nerd-fonts-symbols-mono
ttf-space-mono-nerd

